    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be respectively the sets of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math> for which the system of linear equations<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>has unique solution and infinitely many solutions. Then</p>"
